[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one parser bug, one fix queued. Read report by report,
it holds **three different problems**. The first one is what the ticket says. The other two are
not fixed by that fix. Outcome: parser fixed, hint won't fix (form retired).

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. The parser is fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). The form hint is won't fix, because the booking-v3 form is retired. The one-day moves are counted inside the parser row.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

1. **Parser** ([issue 1](https://github.com/MKurpinski/what-it-shows/issues/1)). The shared parser reads
   every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the day first, so their dates flip. This is the bug in the ticket title.
2. **Form hint** ([issue 2](https://github.com/MKurpinski/what-it-shows/issues/2)). Only on the `booking-v3`
   form, only on the form channel. The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type what it says,
   and the form then reads it the tenant's way. The parser fix does not touch it.
3. **One-day move** ([issue 3](https://github.com/MKurpinski/what-it-shows/issues/3)). The desk read these
   as a move of one day, not a swapped month and day. By tenant they land under `parser`, but the symptom does not match.
   The likely cause is a time zone or day boundary. That is a reading of the report text, not a confirmed cause.

## What the old table showed

The table below is the existing view of #4471. It sorts reports into two causes, so the five one-day
moves still sit inside `parser`, and it says `hint` has no ticket of its own.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. Subjects here are
generic ("Invite came on the wrong day"), so different causes share them. Intake also tagged reports
from the browser locale, which does not say which form or channel a report came through. Many `hint`
reports were tagged `parser`.

## What to do

- Keep three tickets, one per row above. Count each report once, in one of them.
- Check a new date report against its tenant's locale and booking form before you merge it ([triage](/kb/triage/dedupe)).
- Re-read the one-day moves once there are more than five.

